From 92826dae41f575b3b5c45412d1ae5f315ad3fe12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hamza <155834495+lonadonia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:16:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc7: a listing's verdict
 from the products actually accounted for, read the same by every consumer

collection/route_audit.py: a listing is DONE only when every product its counted pages list
has a record of the run placed under the listing (fresh, or excluded with stated reasons),
no organic placement of its own pages is unexpected, every counted page is bound to the
store, and the accounted products reach the highest total the source reported; EMPTY only
with the store's own page stating 0 results; a listing read through subdivisions only by
the union of its subdivisions. Carried, cross-listed, excluded and sponsored products are
counted apart. Until rc6 the coverage file took the larger of the pages' identities and the
listing's own count, and G3 the count: neither looked at the records.

reconciliation: node outcomes, the coverage files and the node coverage rows read the
audit (a listing is keyed by its category source and taxonomy: the same listing can be
planned under two CSV rows). live: the node coverage is synchronised before the gates;
an empty first page keeps its page row. publish: the publication reads the coverage again
from the run's pages, placements and records and refuses an unexplained gap (exit 6), the
pointer and files untouched. checks/contract: products.csv is read as text.
